<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kandyan Convention</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1815</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kandyan Convention was the agreement signed on 2 March 1815 between the British and the chiefs of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandy">Kandy</a>, after they had helped the British depose King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-vikrama-rajasinha">Sri Vikrama Rajasinha</a>. It transferred <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a> over Kandy to the British Crown, making the whole of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceylon">Ceylon</a> a British possession, while promising to protect <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> and the chiefs' rights. A great rebellion against British rule followed in 1817–1818.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kandyan-convention.jpg" alt="Kandyan Convention" width="320" height="269" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Government Archives of Sri Lanka/ Photographed by MediaJet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Kandyan_Convention_of_1815.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
